From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 06:20:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prove the interrupted move's retry reports no collision

The regression test showed the retry finishing the move, the destination in
place and the source gone, but not that it finished it the right way: the
same end state is what a run would show if the retry had mistaken its own
committed copy for another object's, counted a collision and left the source
alone until a later attempt removed it.

It now snapshots ObjectStorageQueueMoveCollisions before the interrupted move
and asserts the counter is unchanged once the retry has removed the source.
The test is parametrized over S3Queue and AzureQueue and over an external
destination, so all four cases carry it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016i1XnLC3KypZdaYYsfzqub
---
 tests/integration/test_storage_s3_queue/test_0.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/integration/test_storage_s3_queue/test_0.py b/tests/integration/test_storage_s3_queue/test_0.py
index 3abf8eaefe4..cf987930603 100644
--- a/tests/integration/test_storage_s3_queue/test_0.py
+++ b/tests/integration/test_storage_s3_queue/test_0.py
@@ -839,6 +839,10 @@ def test_move_retry_recognizes_committed_copy(
         move_to_bucket=destination,
     )
 
+    # The destination the retry finds is the copy the interrupted attempt committed, not another
+    # object's: recognizing it is what must not be counted as a collision.
+    collisions_before = move_collisions(node)
+
     node.query("SYSTEM ENABLE FAILPOINT object_storage_queue_fail_after_move_copy")
     try:
         create_mv(node, table_name, f"{table_name}_dst")
@@ -855,6 +859,8 @@ def test_move_retry_recognizes_committed_copy(
     finally:
         node.query("SYSTEM DISABLE FAILPOINT object_storage_queue_fail_after_move_copy")
 
+    assert move_collisions(node) == collisions_before
+
     if not is_s3:
         metadata = (
             started_cluster.blob_service_client.get_blob_client(
